WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.480
Timo-mo-mo-mo-mo...

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:20.490
You all fail!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.540
Whoops, I fell asleep.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.010
What a weird dream...

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.970
<b>Final Exams</b>

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.970
<b>July 11</b>

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.770
Hibari-chan, how'd it go?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.360
Okay, I guess.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:10.380
How about you, Hanako?

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.730
I answered all the questions.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.850
Really?

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:17.080
Do you two have a minute?

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.160
What is it?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.020
Perhaps I'm being a bit hasty, but...

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.370
Good work, everyone.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.450
We can talk later.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.810
We've now finished all the final 
exams on the basic subjects.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.670
However...

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.920
After lunch, there will be
a special exam for Class 7...

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.090
<b>Special Happiness Test!!</b>

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.090
The "Special Happiness Test."

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.870
Special...?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.920
Ms. Kodaira, no one told us about this!

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.040
Of course not. It's a surprise exam.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.560
What the heck is a "special" test, anyway?

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.480
<b>Report Card</b>

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:56.380
Each semester, we measure your 
practical luck and mental fortune.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:58.280
<b>Spirit
Stamina
Practical Luck 
Mental Fortune
Beauty
Love</b>

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.280
Practical? Mental?

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.490
You'll understand once we get started.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.240
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.240
<b>July 11</b>

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.240
<b>Fighting Final Exams</b>

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.660
This is where we played the dice game.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.920
We haven't been here in a while!

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.460
This time we'll be going even farther down.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.800
No what matter kind of test it is,

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.990
you can count on me to take first place.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.990
There's no way you could do that now.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.200
You were depressed yesterday 
because you're failing.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.830
Shh! Shh!

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.870
You seem to be having fun, Hanako-san.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.710
I wonder what kind of test it is!

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.990
It's so exciting when you don't 
know what's about to happen!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.040
Not knowing what's going 
to be covered on the test

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.820
just makes me nervous.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.570
<b>Class 7 Special Exam Space</b>

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.570
An even deeper underground zone!

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.370
This is where the test will take place.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.540
But there's nothing here...

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.000
Put these on.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.500
My glasses!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.470
Glasses?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.000
They look cool!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.100
They're a measuring tool 
for the happiness test.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.180
Put them on, then press the 
button on the right side.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.140
Welcome to the cyber world.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:10.980
Huh?

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.020
Oh, no! Don't take off your glasses!

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.350
Is this 3D vision?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.400
I've been thinking it for a while now,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.990
but this place clearly isn't a school facility.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.460
Just a peek.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.580
Is this a casino?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.330
It's only virtual.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.060
As one of the nation's distinguished schools,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.270
Tennomifune Academy couldn't 
actually build a casino.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:44.080
Now, Hanakoizumi-san, why don't 
you try playing that game?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.930
Got it!

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.390
<i>Let's play rock-paper-scissors. 
Press any button.</i>

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.360
It's a rock-paper-scissors game!

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.110
<i>Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!</i>

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.600
<b>Lose</b>

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.100
<i>Nope.</i>

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.600
I lost, Ms. Kodaira.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.280
Oh, you did?

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.880
Unfortunately, this will lower 
your score, Hanakoizumi-san.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.730
I have 90 points now.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.120
Your score will be based on your performance.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.790
Each of you will play ten games of chance,

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:13.750
and your points remaining at 
the end will be your grade.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.320
Wh-What kind of crazy test is this?

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.500
This is super fun, Ms. Kodaira!

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.970
Isn't it? Isn't it?

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.470
Shall we get started, then?

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.970
This is a test, right?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.680
From roulette to card games, 
you can play whatever you'd like.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.700
Remember, this is a test,

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.190
so please refrain from 
offering advice to others.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.650
<i>Come on! Let's find your 
lucky four-leaf clover!</i>

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.880
<i>Too bad! No good luck for you.</i>

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.940
<i>Try again! Ha ha ha!</i>

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.830
I can't believe I lost!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.560
Impossible! It must be cheating!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.120
Or it's using some kind of 
special program because

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.590
it fears me, Hagyu Hibiki—

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.590
<b>Whack</b>

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.240
Hibiki, shut up.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.560
Ekoda-san, I appreciate your help 
in keeping the testing area quiet,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.850
but please don't knock out your classmates.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.350
<i>I can see what move it'll use next.</i>

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.310
<b>Rrrumble</b>

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.310
<b>Rrrumble</b>

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.110
Rock, paper, scissors... Shoot!

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.360
<i>Nope!</i>

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:21.730
Shoot!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:21.980
<i>Nope!</i>

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.360
Shoot!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.610
<i>Nope!</i>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.190
Shoot!

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.190
<i>Nope!</i>

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.680
Shoot!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.180
<i>Nope-nope punch!</i>

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.900
<i>One of these chests contains a treasure.</i>

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.080
<b>Click</b>

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.080
<b>Click</b>

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.540
<i>You chose the box on the right!</i>

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.890
Actually, I pushed both at the same time.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.800
You won! Well done, friend!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.160
<i>Take it all!</i>

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.800
Not even machines are immune...

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.790
Oh, too bad.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.310
If they're games of chance, 
there's nothing we can do about it.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.040
Hey, hey. How many games
have you guys played?

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.820
Just one.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.400
Same here. What about you?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.040
Well, I played rock-paper-scissors six times,

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.380
and I have 30 points left.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.790
You lost that much?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:15.660
I guess your first loss at the 
rock-paper-scissors game counted.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.110
Miss, miss.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:18.660
Huh?

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.790
There's a game I would 
like to recommend to you.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.670
It's a special game to help you 
get back the points you lost.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.400
I'll do it! Me, me, me!

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:29.170
Wait!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.360
This is suspicious.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.560
But at this rate, won't Hanako-san 
end up with zero points?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.600
We can play it too, right?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.520
Of course!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.520
Open the door of dreams!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:50.990
Where are we?

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.040
The duel area for competitive games.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:54.740
Duel?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.320
I'll explain while you play.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.600
First you'll have to design your character.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.000
Huh? What?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:04.940
Huh?

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:10.340
Hibarigaoka Ruri-san, 
you'll now choose your job.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.180
Choose whichever clover you like.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.380
All right...

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:15.720
This one, I guess.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.120
I will protect the one I love!

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.510
Wh-Wh-Why am I dressed like this?!

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:43.200
Isn't this more fun? Aren't you happier now?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.890
Your job is knight.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:45.920
You shrank!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.670
I fit in better this way.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.000
You will engage in one-on-one 
combat in this coliseum.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.550
If you win, you can take 30 
points from your opponent.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.090
W-We have to fight?

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:00.560
And here comes your opponent!

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.450
Ekoda-san?

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:08.040
It sounded kind of fun.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.860
I'm a wizard, huh?

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.660
Are you ready?

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.610
First duel!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.280
Ready, go!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.620
Wait! I'm not mentally prepared for this!

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.500
Fire.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.360
I actually made fire.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.670
I'll say it again, but this is just a hologram.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.400
It won't hurt at all.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.440
Yeah, but—

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.330
Sorry.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.040
Unlike Hibiki, I'm not going for first,

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.650
but I don't want to fail, either.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.520
Ice.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:42.970
You want me to fight? Fine!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:46.520
Thunder.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.360
If your clover gauge runs out, you lose.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.070
How's this?

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.360
Hibari-chan!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.160
She blocked it?

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.880
A wizard's strength is 
long-range, offensive spells,

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:20.340
but a knight's strength is a tough defense.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.300
Nice attack.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.310
But...

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.730
Fly.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:37.740
Huh?!

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:38.890
No fair!

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.490
But it is magic.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.250
Meteor Storm.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.040
You must be joking!

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.750
It doesn't hurt, but this is still too intense!

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:06.160
The match is over!

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.330
The winner is Ekoda Ren!

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:13.710
Thirty of Hibarigaoka Ruri-san's points will be transferred to Ekoda Ren-san.

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:16.150
Both of you, make your way 
to the gallery, please.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.630
How did I lose like that?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:26.030
Nice fight. That was fun.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:27.580
You were having fun?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.330
Now, shall we move on to the next match?

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:34.590
Um, may I ask a question?

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:35.900
What is it?

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.320
I don't know about the others,

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:44.650
but if I go out dressed like this,
I'm afraid I may blind someone.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:47.720
We don't allow anyone to cancel their entry.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.260
Hurry, hurry.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:54.090
I see... I feel a bit self-conscious, 
but I suppose I have no choice.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.760
Kumegawa Botan-san, your job is priest.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.480
God will protect me.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.530
That costume seems like it 
would incur God's wrath.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.390
I'm so embarrassed, ashamed, 
and disgusted with myself

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.750
that I wish I could just disappear!

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.850
Your opponent is...

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:16.960
Hagyu Hibiki-san! Your job is archer!

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.830
Hagyu-san...

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.610
How unfortunate for you 
to draw me as your opponent.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.680
I'll show you a victory worthy 
of the top score in our class!

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:28.640
I will defeat you with a single attack!

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:31.600
I'm sorry...

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.660
Second duel! Ready, go!

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.740
<i>She doesn't have anything 
that looks like a weapon.</i>

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.740
Strike first for victory!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.450
I'm sorry!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.430
Botan!

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.120
Did she just hurt herself?

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.830
I need to heal...

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:59.660
Holy light, grant me a miracle.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.550
Of course... She's a priest, 
so she has healing magic...

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.260
Is she taking damage?

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.510
As one who crawls along the ground

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:16.030
and lives in disgrace like a corpse,

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:19.200
it seems that healing magic
has the opposite effect on me...

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.080
You're undead?!

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.230
Undead?

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.700
In any case, it looks like this duel is over.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.910
I will finish you with my most powerful attack!

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:33.120
Hagyu-san, I don't know how to apologize...

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:36.420
There's no need to apologize. This ends now!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.890
Botan!

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.680
Where'd she disappear to?

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:45.230
Show yourself!

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:46.380
Okay.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.310
I'm really sorry.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.720
Ren, people are watching...

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:00.090
She's asleep?

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.520
It was a sleeping spell.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.780
The winner is Kumegawa Botan!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.940
Huh, so that counts as a win, too...

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.080
That was an impressive comeback,

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.450
but wasn't it a bit one-sided?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.910
The outcome of a duel is 
determined by the job matchup.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:21.560
Just as a knight that uses physical 
attacks is weak against a wizard,

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.110
a priest is the mortal enemy of an archer,

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.880
who is weak against mental magic.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:29.970
Oh, so that's why Kumegawa-san 
was apologizing so much.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:34.690
She knew she could take 
out Hibiki at any time.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.930
I kind of feel bad for her.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.680
The cats are watching, too...

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.690
The next match is the last!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.740
Here comes Hanakoizumi Anne!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.470
Beat out the rhythm of the four-leaf clover!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.820
May my steps of happiness reach out to you!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.850
The dance of blooming flowers...

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.960
Hanako Happiness!

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:58.090
Let's dance together!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:02.090
Okay, Hanakoizumi Anne-san.

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:03.820
Your job is dancer.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.460
Wow, I'm a dancer!

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.920
And your opponent is...

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.080
What's wrong?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.140
Uh...

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:21.080
Oh, it seems all the others have 
finished their ten games. Tee-hee.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.020
What?!

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.980
Oh, no! Isn't there anything you can do?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.570
If that's the case, we have no choice.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.530
Hanakoizumi-san, I will be your opponent.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.870
You will?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.240
No matter who your opponent is,

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:42.490
the randomness of your job and 
the point system won't change.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.500
That's true.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.940
Thank you, Ms. Kodaira!

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.250
Not at all.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.970
I'll choose this clover.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.520
Oh, I'm a black knight.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.300
<i>That looks super evil...</i>

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.490
Oh, right. How's the job matchup?

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:14.200
You'll find out once we start fighting.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:20.660
Final duel! Ready, go!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.870
Here we go!

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:25.740
How does a dancer fight?

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.590
In games, they increase 
their stats by dancing.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.230
She's just fighting normally.

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.390
Hanako, try dancing!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.140
Huh?

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.740
Oh, right!

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.100
Ahoy-hoy, hoy-hoy!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:44.970
That's not quite right.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:48.060
This is going to drive us crazy...

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:53.920
<i>The highly offensive black knight</i>

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.260
<i>is weak against the dancer's mental attacks,</i>

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:59.500
<i>but I can't hold back.</i>

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.790
<i>I will aim to finish this quickly.</i>

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:04.540
Hanako-san!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.610
Hanakoizumi-san, you currently have 30 points.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:12.380
If you lose this duel, you'll lose 
30 points, leaving you with zero.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.830
And a score of zero is unacceptable.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.570
You'll have to take extra classes.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:21.180
You'll have to come to school 
every day over summer break!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.100
What?!

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:30.280
We're in the middle of an exam, Kumegawa-san.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:34.280
I can't allow Hanako-san to take extra classes.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.820
If... If she does...

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:44.660
She won't be able to hang out 
with us over summer break!

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.340
I've already come up with a day-by-day schedule!

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:48.180
Really?

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:50.120
I was planning to discuss it with you both later!

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:51.380
That's a bit hasty!

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:56.790
I'd rather join Hanako-san than 
spend summer break without her!

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:02.350
I see. Then I'll have to punish you.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.180
Botan-chan...

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.810
We'll die together.

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:12.710
Hibari-chan!

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.130
I can't believe you two.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.950
You owe me a super jumbo parfait!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:18.570
Sure!

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.780
Oh, my. You too, Hibarigaoka-san?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.990
How reckless of you!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.620
What are they doing?

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.630
This has nothing to do with the test anymore.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:36.860
Let's work together.

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:37.760
Yeah!

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.590
We're like a real party.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:45.020
That looks fun.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.270
Huh? You're not gonna...

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:49.790
Ugh! I knew it!

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:50.730
Meteor Storm.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.720
Don't blame me for whatever happens!

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.000
Why don't you just watch, then?

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.910
Don't leave me out!

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.120
You can do it, guys!

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.280
I feel stronger...

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:10.810
She boosted their stats!

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.000
Okay!

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.390
Ahoy-hoy!

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.020
I can't believe you people.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.360
What do you think this important 
test is supposed to be?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.070
Ahoy-hoy!

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.710
I'll have to teach all of you!

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:42.680
What is that?

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:43.530
A demon?

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:50.300
I saw this in my dream.

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:55.720
Bring it on, you reckless fools!

00:19:55.720 --> 00:20:00.980
I'll [meow] your ridiculous 
[woof woof] and [roar] you!

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:07.810
Guys!

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:10.910
That should've protected us...

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:12.680
A guard-piercing spell...

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:14.300
She's too strong.

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:16.270
We can't do this...

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.530
What do we do?

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.290
Don't give up yet!

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.240
Timothy...

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.030
It's time to change classes, everyone!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:26.940
Huh?

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:29.750
Here we go!

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:39.790
This is the special valkyrie job.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.160
How stylish!

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.720
It has a class advantage against demons.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.040
So the rest is up to us, right?

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:48.260
Don't let up!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:51.180
Timothy!

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.380
This is incredible!

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.300
Everyone, use a combo attack!

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:01.440
We can do that?

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:05.100
If you shout an ability name, it'll happen. 
Just come up with something.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.410
I-I can't do something so embarrassing!

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.370
Okay! Lucky!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.170
Huh?

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.120
Someone say the next word.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.240
Happy.

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.210
Huh?

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:15.920
Miracle!

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:17.360
Sheesh...

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.630
All right, Love!

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.900
Love?

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.630
A-Attack!

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:29.970
Lucky Happy Miracle Love Attack!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:43.480
What is this power?!

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.640
Not... bad...

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:52.620
I may have lost my cool there.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:03.160
As a penalty, I'm taking all your points.

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:04.010
Yes, ma'am...

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:05.750
Furthermore...

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.240
I'm redistributing the ten points I took

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:11.230
from Hanakoizumi-san during the demo

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:14.300
between the four of you.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:18.190
Now no one has zero points.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:19.880
But why?

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:25.860
Because luck isn't determined 
by the strength of an individual.

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:28.650
It changes with all kinds of factors, including

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:31.060
your surroundings and the people around you.

00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:35.720
Your actions today weren't totally incorrect.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.420
It doesn't matter if you 
don't understand right now.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.720
In any case, you don't have 
to take summer classes.

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.900
Isn't that enough for you girls?

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:48.640
That's great!

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:50.420
Let's have lots of fun together!

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:53.550
Yeah! Let's hang out over summer break!

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:55.740
That was a fun test.

00:22:57.330 --> 00:22:59.060
Thanks, everyone!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>July 13</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>A Stormy Group Lesson</b>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:43.020
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
